### Comprehensive List of Reporting Requirements in the NSQHS Standards for Acute Services

#### **1. Clinical Governance Standard**
- **Incident Reporting**: Health services must have systems in place to report and manage clinical incidents, including adverse events and near misses [1](https://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/sites/default/files/2021-05/national_safety_and_quality_health_service_nsqhs_standards_second_edition_-_updated_may_2021.pdf).
- **Performance Reporting**: Regular reporting on key performance indicators (KPIs) related to patient safety and quality of care [1](https://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/sites/default/files/2021-05/national_safety_and_quality_health_service_nsqhs_standards_second_edition_-_updated_may_2021.pdf).

#### **2. Partnering with Consumers Standard**
- **Consumer Feedback**: Reporting on consumer feedback and complaints to improve service delivery and patient experience [1](https://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/sites/default/files/2021-05/national_safety_and_quality_health_service_nsqhs_standards_second_edition_-_updated_may_2021.pdf).

#### **3. Preventing and Controlling Infections Standard**
- **Infection Surveillance**: Reporting on healthcare-associated infections (HAIs) to monitor and control infection rates [1](https://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/sites/default/files/2021-05/national_safety_and_quality_health_service_nsqhs_standards_second_edition_-_updated_may_2021.pdf).
- **Antimicrobial Stewardship**: Reporting on the use of antimicrobials to ensure appropriate use and reduce resistance [1](https://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/sites/default/files/2021-05/national_safety_and_quality_health_service_nsqhs_standards_second_edition_-_updated_may_2021.pdf).

#### **4. Medication Safety Standard**
- **Medication Incidents**: Reporting medication errors and adverse drug reactions to improve medication safety [1](https://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/sites/default/files/2021-05/national_safety_and_quality_health_service_nsqhs_standards_second_edition_-_updated_may_2021.pdf).

#### **5. Comprehensive Care Standard**
- **Care Planning and Delivery**: Reporting on the implementation and outcomes of comprehensive care plans for patients [1](https://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/sites/default/files/2021-05/national_safety_and_quality_health_service_nsqhs_standards_second_edition_-_updated_may_2021.pdf).

#### **6. Communicating for Safety Standard**
- **Communication Incidents**: Reporting communication failures that impact patient safety, such as handover errors[1](https://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/sites/default/files/2021-05/national_safety_and_quality_health_service_nsqhs_standards_second_edition_-_updated_may_2021.pdf).

#### **7. Blood Management Standard**
- **Blood Product Usage**: Reporting on the use and management of blood products to ensure safety and efficiency[1](https://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/sites/default/files/2021-05/national_safety_and_quality_health_service_nsqhs_standards_second_edition_-_updated_may_2021.pdf).

#### **8. Recognising and Responding to Acute Deterioration Standard**
- **Deterioration Incidents**: Reporting incidents where there was a failure to recognize or respond to acute deterioration in patients [1](https://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/sites/default/files/2021-05/national_safety_and_quality_health_service_nsqhs_standards_second_edition_-_updated_may_2021.pdf).

These reporting requirements are designed to protect the public from harm and improve the quality of health service provision by ensuring that relevant systems are in place to meet expected standards of safety and quality [1](https://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/sites/default/files/2021-05/national_safety_and_quality_health_service_nsqhs_standards_second_edition_-_updated_may_2021.pdf).

